"Help.01" = "Open a font, or drag one onto the app's window or Dock icon. Recently opened items are supported.";
"Help.02" = "Use the menu bar to copy the font open in the current window to your user Fonts folder in one click.";
"Help.03" = "When you open a variable font, a variation panel appears beside the window controls. Drag it out to keep it open. Select a numeric value and use ↑/↓ or ⇧↑/⇧↓ to adjust it.";
"Help.04" = "Type one or more characters in the sidebar to see all associated glyphs. Use ⌥⏎ to insert a line break. You can also right-click and choose “Saved Text” to save the current text or quickly enter text you’ve saved before.";
"Help.05" = "Double-click a glyph, or select it and press ⏎, to replace the default glyph and show its alternates. Hold ⇧ while doing this to add the glyph.";
"Help.06" = "Use ↑/↓ to move between glyphs, ⌘↑/⌘↓ to move between base glyphs, and ⌥↑/⌥↓ to jump to the first or last glyph in the list.";
"Help.07" = "Use ⌘C to copy all encoded characters of the selected glyph.";
"Help.08" = "Hover over a Unicode badge to see the character name defined by the Unicode standard.";
"Help.09" = "All Glyphs is the default. Right-click to switch views, or press ⌘1 for Single Glyph, ⌘2 for Multi-Character, or ⌘3 for All Glyphs.";
"Help.10" = "In Multi-Character, click a glyph to view its alternates. Typography in the View and context menus lists the font’s native features: checkmarks indicate selected options; exclusive groups allow only one choice. Use ⌘5 to switch vertical writing. Underline ⌘U and Strikethrough ⌘L apply to the entire multi-character preview. Writing Direction appears in View when CoreText reports support for a right-to-left language. Text Decorations > Outline ⌘Y reveals contours retained in the font, including overlaps. Typesetting Language lists the font’s GSUB language tags, deduplicated across scripts. It is hidden when no named language system is declared.";
"Help.11" = "In All Glyphs, double-click a glyph to add it to the existing text. Clicking a glyph in the sidebar also makes it blink there.";
"Help.12" = "Use ⌘+/⌘− to zoom the glyphs, and ⌥⌘+/⌥⌘− to increase or decrease the margins in Multi-Character. Trackpad pinch also works.";
"Help.13" = "The shadow indicates the glyph's width and height, as well as the layout's line height and leading; press ⌘4 to hide it.";
"Help.14" = "Dark mode is supported, but be careful: clicking a solid glyph can dazzle you.";

